fix: inject missing layout CSS into 7 problematic sections

Sections affected: custom-columns, slideshow-hero, collage,
multirow, parallax-hero, bundle-deals, pricing-table.

Root cause: these sections relied on CSS classes (.custom-columns,
.hero-slide, .collage, .image-with-text, .plan-card, etc.) that
were defined in the source theme's base.css but missing from Seqes.

Changes:
- Add common utility CSS to theme.liquid (page-width, grid, media,
  card, button, field, select, popup, rte, and visibility helpers)
- Extract and inject section-specific layout CSS from source theme
  into each section's style block (custom-columns grid, hero slides,
  collage layout, multirow image-with-text, parallax positioning)
- Ensure dedicated CSS assets are linked (section-bundle-deals.css,
  section-pricing-table.css, collage.css)
